{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nMr. Chanek has an integer represented by a string $$$s$$$. Zero or more digits have been erased and are denoted by the character _. There are also zero or more digits marked by the character X, meaning they're the same digit.Mr. Chanek wants to count the number of possible integer $$$s$$$, where $$$s$$$ is divisible by $$$25$$$. Of course, $$$s$$$ must not contain any leading zero. He can replace the character _ with any digit. He can also replace the character X with any digit, but it must be the same for every character X.As a note, a leading zero is any 0 digit that comes before the first nonzero digit in a number string in positional notation. For example, 0025 has two leading zeroes. An exception is the integer zero, (0 has no leading zero, but 0000 has three leading zeroes).\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class B {\n\n    public static int takeInt(BufferedReader br) throws IOException {\n        return Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n    }\n\n    public static String[] takeStrings(BufferedReader br) throws IOException {\n        return br.readLine().trim().split(\" \");\n    }\n\n    public static int[] takeInts(BufferedReader br) throws IOException {\n        String[] inp = takeStrings(br);\n        int[] arr = new int[inp.length];\n        for (int i = 0; i < inp.length; i++) {\n            arr[i] = Integer.parseInt(inp[i]);\n        }\n        return arr;\n    }\n\n    public static char[] generateStrings(char[] str, int n, char dig) {\n        char[] result = new char[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            result[i] = (str[i] == 'X') ? dig : str[i];\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        int test = 1;\n        StringBuilder ans = new StringBuilder();\n        outer: while (test-- > 0) {\n            char[] str = br.readLine().trim().toCharArray();\n            int n = str.length;\n\n            if (n == 1) {\n                if ((str[0] == '0' || str[0] == '_') || str[0] == 'X' || str[0] == '1') {\n                    ans.append(1).append(\"\\n\");\n                    continue;\n                }\n            }\n\n            long cnt = 0;\n            boolean hasX = false;\n            for (char c : str) if (c == 'X') hasX = true;\n\n            if (hasX) {\n                for (char ch = '0'; ch <= '9'; ch++) {\n                    cnt += solve(generateStrings(str, n, ch), n);\n                }\n            } else {\n                cnt += solve(str, n);\n            }\n\n            ans.append(cnt).append(\"\\n\");\n        }\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n\n    public static long cal(char[] str, String suffix, int n, int un) {\n        if (n < 2) return 0;\n        char last = suffix.charAt(1);\n        char first = suffix.charAt(0);\n        if ((str[n - 1] == '_' || str[n - 1] == last) &&\n            (str[n - 2] == '_' || str[n - 2] == first)) {\n            return (long) Math.pow(10, un);\n        }\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    public static long solve(char[] str, int n) {\n        if (n == 1 || str[0] == '0') return 0;\n\n        int un = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i < n - 2; i++) if (str[i] == '_') ++un;\n\n        long cnt = 0;\n        cnt += cal(str, \"25\", n, un);\n        cnt += cal(str, \"50\", n, un);\n        cnt += cal(str, \"75\", n, un);\n\n        if (n > 2 && str[0] == '_') cnt *= 9L;\n\n        if (n >= 3) {\n            if ((str[n - 1] == '_' || str[n - 1] == '0') &&\n                (str[n - 2] == '_' || str[n - 2] == '0')) {\n                if (n > 3) {\n                    long temp = (long) Math.pow(10, un);\n                    if (str[0] == '_') temp *= 9L;\n                    cnt += temp;\n                } else if (n == 3) {\n                    if (str[0] == '_') cnt += 9;\n                    else cnt += 1;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        return cnt;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class B {\n\n    public static int takeInt(BufferedReader br) throws IOException {\n        return Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n    }\n\n    public static String[] takeStrings(BufferedReader br) throws IOException {\n        return br.readLine().trim().split(\" \");\n    }\n\n    public static int[] takeInts(BufferedReader br) throws IOException {\n        String[] inp = takeStrings(br);\n        int[] arr = new int[inp.length];\n        for (int i = 0; i < inp.length; i++) {\n            arr[i] = Integer.parseInt(inp[i]);\n        }\n        return arr;\n    }\n\n    public static char[] generateStrings(char[] str, char digit) {\n        char[] result = new char[str.length];\n        for (int i = 0; i < str.length; i++) {\n            if (str[i] == 'X') {\n                result[i] = digit;\n            } else {\n                result[i] = str[i];\n            }\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        int test = 1;\n        StringBuilder ans = new StringBuilder();\n        \n        while (test-- > 0) {\n            char[] str = br.readLine().trim().toCharArray();\n            int n = str.length;\n\n            long cnt = 0;\n            boolean hasX = false;\n            for (char c : str) {\n                if (c == 'X') {\n                    hasX = true;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n\n            if (hasX) {\n                for (char ch = '0'; ch <= '9'; ch++) {\n                    cnt += solve(generateStrings(str, ch), n);\n                }\n            } else {\n                cnt += solve(str, n);\n            }\n\n            ans.append(cnt).append(\"\\n\");\n        }\n        System.out.print(ans);\n    }\n\n    public static long solve(char[] str, int n) {\n        // Check for leading zero\n        if (str[0] == '0') return 0;\n        if (str[0] == '_' && n > 1) return 0; // leading underscore is not allowed for multi-digit numbers\n\n        long count = 0;\n\n        // Try all possible endings for divisibility by 25: 00, 25, 50, 75\n        String[] endings = {\"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"};\n\n        for (String end : endings) {\n            char last = end.charAt(1);\n            char secondLast = end.charAt(0);\n\n            // Check if last two digits can match the ending\n            if ((str[n-1] == '_' || str[n-1] == last) &&\n                (str[n-2] == '_' || str[n-2] == secondLast)) {\n                \n                // Count the number of underscores in positions other than last two\n                int freeDigits = 0;\n                for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {\n                    if (str[i] == '_') freeDigits++;\n                }\n\n                // Calculate possibilities for the first digit\n                long firstDigitOptions = 1;\n                if (str[0] == '_') {\n                    if (n == 1) {\n                        firstDigitOptions = 1; // single digit case handled separately\n                    } else {\n                        firstDigitOptions = 9; // 1-9 for first digit if it's underscore\n                    }\n                } else if (str[0] != 'X') {\n                    // If it's a fixed digit, it must be non-zero for multi-digit numbers\n                    if (n > 1 && str[0] == '0') {\n                        continue; // invalid leading zero\n                    }\n                }\n\n                // For positions with 'X', they are already fixed in generateStrings, so no additional options\n                // For underscores, each has 10 possibilities\n                long total = firstDigitOptions;\n                for (int i = 0; i < freeDigits; i++) {\n                    total *= 10;\n                }\n\n                count += total;\n            }\n        }\n\n        return count;\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.3841830625315197e-06, -3.313963316031732e-05, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.777537883957848e-05, -2.6464111215318553e-05, -0.003600069787353277, -4.1483970562694594e-05, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -4.255681051290594e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -6.317892984952778e-05, -5.483612312673358e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.00015293381875380874, -2.9682672902708873e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -9.77468371274881e-05, -8.34461570775602e-06, -0.4862661361694336, -0.0001565095444675535, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -5.245195097813848e-06, -1.156323378381785e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -1.2278481335670222e-05, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -8.344646857949556e-0